  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「リンゴ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%AA%E3%83%B3%E3%82%B4",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 111214394,
      "text": "リンゴ は、バラ科リンゴ属の落葉高木の一種、またはその果実（図1）のこと。作物群としては花托が肥大した部分を食用とする仁果類（仁果果実）に分類される果樹（果実）である。植物学上の和名では、セイヨウリンゴともよばれる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Apple」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1378395484,
      "text": "An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."
    }
  },
